function Room({ roomId }) {
  useEffect(() => {
    console.log(`Connected to ${roomId}`);

    return () => {
      console.log(`Disconnected from ${roomId}`);
    };
  }, [roomId]);

  return <p>Room: {roomId}</p>;
}
```

The Effect reads `roomId`, so `roomId` belongs in the dependency list.

